<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Guide mode areas (docs/HELP.md): area = the id a screen registers in GuideRegistry; screen = where it shows (Any = everywhere). -->
  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_terminal_status</defName>
    <label>Bottom bar</label>
    <area>terminal.status</area>
    <screen>Any</screen>
    <order>90</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Heat_Netsick</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Always in sight: your trace (Heat) with its level, the network, Netsick and the latest trace event.</text>
        <hint>click the trace bar to open the Heat screen.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_onboarding_list</defName>
    <label>Getting online</label>
    <area>onboarding.list</area>
    <screen>Onboarding</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Start</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>These steps bring your colony online. Done steps turn green; the yellow one is next.</text>
      </li>
      <li>
        <text>When all are done, the Core opens and its nodes unlock one by one. "Skip" shows the full Core right away.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_core_map</defName>
    <label>Node map</label>
    <area>core.map</area>
    <screen>Core</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Start_Terminal</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Each node is a part of your network: Club, Board, Archive, Server room, Studio, Gateway. Badges count what needs attention.</text>
      </li>
      <li>
        <text>A glowing node has news. Locked nodes show a lock: hover to see how they open.</text>
        <hint>click any node.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_core_ring</defName>
    <label>Heat ring</label>
    <area>core.ring</area>
    <screen>Core</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Heat</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Your trace: five arcs for five levels, the marker at the current value, the number and the trend for the last day.</text>
        <hint>click the ring to open "Heat and trace".</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_core_now</defName>
    <label>Now</label>
    <area>core.now</area>
    <screen>Core</screen>
    <order>3</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Start_Terminal</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>One main recommendation: what is worth doing right now. The buttons under it lead to the right node.</text>
        <hint>press one of its buttons.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_core_alerts</defName>
    <label>Alerts</label>
    <area>core.alerts</area>
    <screen>Core</screen>
    <order>4</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Events</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>What is burning: escaping AIs, deadlines, hijacked turrets, requests. Red is urgent; a click leads to the node.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_core_colony</defName>
    <label>Colony online</label>
    <area>core.colony</area>
    <screen>Core</screen>
    <order>5</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Start_Terminal</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Your network resources: cyberdata, AIs and slots, braindance chips, the hacker group's favor.</text>
      </li>
      <li>
        <text>Below: the energy the network draws, when new Gateway nodes come and when the corporate core appears.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_heat_hero</defName>
    <label>Value and scale</label>
    <area>heat.hero</area>
    <screen>Heat</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Heat_Levels</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Your Heat and its level, the change over 7 days and today's cooling.</text>
      </li>
      <li>
        <text>The scale shows all five levels. Hover a segment for its effects; click it to show them in "Level effects".</text>
        <hint>click a segment.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_heat_graph</defName>
    <label>Graph</label>
    <area>heat.graph</area>
    <screen>Heat</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Heat</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Heat over the last week or day (switch top right). Dots are events: green scrubs, yellow dives, red hacks.</text>
      </li>
      <li>
        <text>Move the mouse over the graph to read the value at that moment; click a dot to open the Archive.</text>
        <hint>hover over a dot.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_heat_effects</defName>
    <label>Level effects</label>
    <area>heat.effects</area>
    <screen>Heat</screen>
    <order>3</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Heat_Levels</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>What the level brings: threats that can come and how cooling changes. Below: how long until the level drops.</text>
      </li>
      <li>
        <text>"Cyberpedia ↗" opens the article about all levels.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_heat_lower</defName>
    <label>How to lower</label>
    <area>heat.lower</area>
    <screen>Heat</screen>
    <order>4</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Heat_Lower</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Through a fixer: each fixer of the pool with their rate. "Call" opens a channel, "Scrub…" opens the scrub window for that fixer.</text>
        <hint>call a fixer and scrub a little.</hint>
      </li>
      <li>
        <text>A Ghost AI can wipe the trace too (dimmed if you have none). Or just wait: Heat cools every day.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_heat_raised</defName>
    <label>What raised it</label>
    <area>heat.raised</area>
    <screen>Heat</screen>
    <order>5</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Heat</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>The biggest sources of Heat this week and the totals: gained, scrubbed, cooled. Click a row to open the Archive.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_club_group</defName>
    <label>Hacker group</label>
    <area>club.group</area>
    <screen>Club</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Group</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Favor from cyberspace finds. At full favor, "Call the group" sends allied fighters (or advanced cyberdata without allies).</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_club_pinned</defName>
    <label>Pinned contacts</label>
    <area>club.pinned</area>
    <screen>Club</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Fixers_Pool</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Fixers with high reputation stay for good: their trait is known and their prices are the best.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_club_pool</defName>
    <label>The pool</label>
    <area>club.pool</area>
    <screen>Club</screen>
    <order>3</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Fixers_Pool</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>The rotating pool and when it changes next. Unpinned fixers leave at the rotation unless you hold them.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_club_card</defName>
    <label>A fixer's card</label>
    <area>club.card</area>
    <screen>Club</screen>
    <order>4</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Fixers_Types</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Specialty and trait chips, the reputation bar with the pin mark.</text>
      </li>
      <li>
        <text>Call (silver opens a channel), Scrub the trace, Shop. Top right: Hold for a fee per rotation, or Break ties.</text>
        <hint>call this fixer.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_board_active</defName>
    <label>Active contracts</label>
    <area>board.active</area>
    <screen>Board</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Fixers_Contracts</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>What you took: progress, deadline and the reward. A missed deadline costs reputation.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_board_offers</defName>
    <label>Offers</label>
    <area>board.offers</area>
    <screen>Board</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Fixers_Contracts</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Contracts your fixers offer. Accept one; silent fixers show when they will talk again.</text>
        <hint>accept an offer.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_archive_list</defName>
    <label>Trace log</label>
    <area>archive.list</area>
    <screen>Archive</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Heat</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Every change of your Heat, newest first: what happened and by how much. Hover a row for the full text.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_studio_summary</defName>
    <label>Summary</label>
    <area>studio.summary</area>
    <screen>Studio</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Braindance</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Goggles in the colony, chips in storage and raw recordings waiting.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_studio_records</defName>
    <label>Raw recordings</label>
    <area>studio.records</area>
    <screen>Studio</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_BD_Record</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Recordings made with the goggles. Edit one into a chip: pick the mood and wait for the work.</text>
        <hint>edit a recording.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_studio_library</defName>
    <label>Chip library</label>
    <area>studio.library</area>
    <screen>Studio</screen>
    <order>3</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_BD_Chips</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Finished chips with their mood and quality. Black chips are stronger and riskier.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_studio_hooked</defName>
    <label>Dependency</label>
    <area>studio.hooked</area>
    <screen>Studio</screen>
    <order>4</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_BD_Black</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Colonists with braindance tolerance or addiction. Without regular braindance an addict gets withdrawal.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_server_list</defName>
    <label>Your AIs</label>
    <area>server.list</area>
    <screen>Server</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_AI</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Every AI by where it lives: the server, a coprocessor, a host.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_server_card</defName>
    <label>An AI's card</label>
    <area>server.card</area>
    <screen>Server</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_AI_Feeding</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Status, archetype, trust and hunger.</text>
      </li>
      <li>
        <text>"Eats" shows its food and how long it stays fed; the request plate shows what it asks, the deadline and the stakes.</text>
        <hint>hover over the request.</hint>
      </li>
      <li>
        <text>Buttons: feed, use its service (costs trust and hunger), move it to a host or a coprocessor, isolate or erase.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_field</defName>
    <label>Node field</label>
    <area>gateway.field</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Nodes</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>External nodes in cyberspace. Bigger circles pay more; grey ones are hidden.</text>
        <hint>drag the field, scroll to zoom, middle mouse to reset.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_zoom</defName>
    <label>Camera</label>
    <area>gateway.zoom</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Zoom in, zoom out and reset the camera (or press the middle mouse button on the field).</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_node</defName>
    <label>The node</label>
    <area>gateway.node</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>3</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Rewards</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>The selected node: type, defense, ICE, trace per action and risk.</text>
        <hint>click a node on the field.</hint>
      </li>
      <li>
        <text>Reward: the multiplier of the dive cost and what you can bring back, item by item.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_programs</defName>
    <label>Programs and daemons</label>
    <area>gateway.programs</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>4</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Programs</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Load programs into the pod's slots before diving; each costs cyberdata. Daemons are always on.</text>
        <hint>toggle a program.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_dive</defName>
    <label>Dive</label>
    <area>gateway.dive</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>5</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Dive</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>The total cost (hover for the breakdown) and the DIVE button: a netrunner must lie in a powered pod.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_gateway_search</defName>
    <label>Search and view</label>
    <area>gateway.search</area>
    <screen>Gateway</screen>
    <order>6</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Find hidden nodes for cyberdata, switch between circles and a list, and see when new nodes come.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_dive_steps</defName>
    <label>Node steps</label>
    <area>dive.steps</area>
    <screen>Dive</screen>
    <order>1</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Dive</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>The way from the lobby to the exit: gates to hack, ICE, files and memory. The bright one is where you are; ✓ passed, ■ blocked, ? hidden.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_dive_fork</defName>
    <label>Fork</label>
    <area>dive.fork</area>
    <screen>Dive</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Dive</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>At a fork the way splits: the hard path pays more but Black ICE guards it and the trace is louder; the easy path is quiet, pays less and hides a passage. Scan to see the numbers; the choice is final and costs no action.</text>
        <hint>a prepared runner (good hacker, Sword, Shield) gains on the hard path; a novice is better off on the easy one.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_dive_actions</defName>
    <label>Actions</label>
    <area>dive.actions</area>
    <screen>Dive</screen>
    <order>2</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Dive</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Your actions this turn (dots). Move, scan, hack, download, exit; each raises the dive's trace. Exit leaves at once.</text>
        <hint>hover over Hack to see the chance.</hint>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_dive_gauges</defName>
    <label>Turn and trace</label>
    <area>dive.gauges</area>
    <screen>Dive</screen>
    <order>3</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Heat</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Turns left before the node throws you out, and the trace that becomes Heat when you leave.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_dive_programs</defName>
    <label>Programs</label>
    <area>dive.programs</area>
    <screen>Dive</screen>
    <order>4</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Programs</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Loaded programs with charges left and your daemons. Spent charges dim.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_dive_haul</defName>
    <label>Haul</label>
    <area>dive.haul</area>
    <screen>Dive</screen>
    <order>5</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Rewards</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>What you carry so far. A retreat from deep inside loses part of it.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_dive_log</defName>
    <label>Log</label>
    <area>dive.log</area>
    <screen>Dive</screen>
    <order>6</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Dive</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>The dive's terminal: every action and the node's answer, newest at the bottom.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

  <Netrun.GuideAreaDef>
    <defName>NR_Guide_dive_retreat</defName>
    <label>Retreat</label>
    <area>dive.retreat</area>
    <screen>Dive</screen>
    <order>7</order>
    <helpPage>NR_Help_Gateway_Dive</helpPage>
    <steps>
      <li>
        <text>Leave the dive early. From the lobby it is free; deeper you lose part of the haul.</text>
      </li>
    </steps>
  </Netrun.GuideAreaDef>

</Defs>
